      "result_description": "Wadebridge CC - 1st XI - Won",
      "result_applied_to": "36578",
      "match_notes": "Wadebridge continued their fine start to the season with a 112-run success at home to Lanhydrock. Openers James Maycock (58) and Matt Jolliffe (41) laid a strong platform with a hundred stand before 4 quick wickets, 3 to the spin of Reuben Turner (3-20) pegged back the hosts. But Neil Richards (57*) provided an expert finishers role for the Swans as they amassed 226-9, Caleb Rowe taking 3-37 at the death. In reply Elliot Dunnett (3-21) soon had the visitors in trouble before Jake Carter (55) and Tom Trethewey (33) formed a solid stand. Once they were parted the end came swiftly though, as the last 6 wickets fell for just 11 runs as Lanhydrock were dismissed for 114, spinners Cal Morse (3-20) and Alek Gill (3-21) causing havoc to maintain the Bridgers unbeaten start.",
